            <div xml:id="d860">

                <pb facs="0805" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2238: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Butrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-04T17:00:00+09:00">September 4, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 4—6:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>869. Glassford will shortly resume informal conversations with Iwamura, informing
                    him that we propose to carry out compromise decision of Shanghai Defense
                    Committee at early date and requesting <pb facs="0806" n="798" xml:id="pg798"/>
                    agreement. Minor modifications may develop from conversations which will be
                    acceptable to both sides.</p>
                <p>Hart here.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Butrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
